yinliang: measure the power press, and replay the power-off chord

PRIVATE YINLIANG BRANCH PATCH - no numeric prefix, same rule as the
WLED backlight patch: mainline numbers belong to the WiFi/GPU AI.

Evidence (boot-01-keys-0299.txt): a short press locks and wakes, so the
HID path is complete; a long press is measured and launches Siri
(exec Siri, L4682), which is what a real iPhone does with Siri on; and
the real iPhone X chord - power + volume held together for ~2 s
(L4688-L4973) - produced no slider. The events are therefore correct
and the missing piece is on the SpringBoard side, not in this driver.

So this patch stops adding events and starts measuring them:
  SWEET KEYS: power held <n> ms (<r> repeat(s), <c> chord(s))
  SWEET KEYS: chord power+volume<k> down

Plus one knob to replay the chord with exact timing, BOTH DEFAULT OFF:
  sweetkeys_off=<ms>       hold a synthetic volume key for 2.5 s
  sweetkeys_offkey=1|2     1 = volume up, 2 = volume down (default 2)
  sweetkeys_hold=<ms>      negative control, expected to do nothing

Also fixed: a failed SPMI read used to report volume-up as pressed and
leave it stuck down (uint8_t 0 + !(0 & 1u) == 1); the previous state is
carried instead.

Apply AFTER 0062 -> 0245 -> 0294 v2 -> WLED backlight.
Touches only sweet_keys.c and SweetHID.cpp. Zero WiFi files.

